WEBVTT

00:00.953 --> 00:07.625
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.953 --> 00:07.625
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.689 --> 00:14.716
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.689 --> 00:14.716
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.301 --> 00:21.973
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.301 --> 00:21.973
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.998 --> 00:28.212
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.998 --> 00:28.212
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.106 --> 00:34.778
This surging power...

00:29.106 --> 00:34.778
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.106 --> 00:31.193
Black Jack

00:36.280 --> 00:42.535
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.280 --> 00:42.535
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.329 --> 00:48.291
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.329 --> 00:48.291
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.862 --> 00:57.217
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.862 --> 00:57.217
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.718 --> 00:59.409
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.409 --> 01:01.402
will be there

01:01.422 --> 01:04.382
It makes me glad...

01:01.422 --> 01:04.382
yokatta

01:04.627 --> 01:12.107
That I found my place here.

01:04.627 --> 01:12.107
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.160 --> 01:13.678
Oh WISDOM

01:13.678 --> 01:15.527
will be there

01:15.555 --> 01:18.196
I searched for the reason

01:15.555 --> 01:18.196
sagashita

01:18.197 --> 01:25.245
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.197 --> 01:25.245
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.830 --> 01:32.710
as long as we're alive.

01:25.870 --> 01:32.710
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.711 --> 01:34.796
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.880 --> 01:37.064
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.216 --> 01:39.827
His name is Black Jack.

01:51.907 --> 01:55.085
Originally "Chronically Laughing" by Tezuka Osamu

01:51.907 --> 01:55.085
The Chronically Laughing Classmate

01:57.797 --> 01:59.589
It's the best!

01:59.590 --> 02:01.758
Mr. Principal!

02:01.759 --> 02:02.968
A real pal!

02:01.759 --> 02:02.945
Title says: Mr. Principal: A Real Pal!

02:02.969 --> 02:03.844
Mr. Principal!

02:03.845 --> 02:04.970
A real pal!

02:04.971 --> 02:06.304
Mr. Principal!

02:06.305 --> 02:08.890
A real pal!

02:11.477 --> 02:13.181
Pinoco-chan,

02:13.521 --> 02:15.856
we're disturbing him while he's working.

02:20.194 --> 02:22.216
Pinoco-chan...

02:22.568 --> 02:23.908
Why stop laughing?

02:27.076 --> 02:30.078
Only intelligent animals are capable of laughter.

02:30.638 --> 02:32.549
So laugh all you can.

02:36.753 --> 02:39.276
Ohmigewdness!

03:04.322 --> 03:06.209
Therefore...

03:26.844 --> 03:29.012
Man, it's Gera again.

03:29.013 --> 03:30.764
What's so funny?

03:30.765 --> 03:36.478
In the morning meeting, Mr. Principal said "Our pal"!

03:41.734 --> 03:44.444
<i>The student's nickname was Gera.</i>

03:45.279 --> 03:48.358
<i>It came from the fact that he was always laughing.</i>

03:48.991 --> 03:52.867
<i>Once he started, his laughter could
be heard throughout the campus,</i>

03:53.287 --> 03:58.625
<i>and I guess it made other students want to laugh as well.</i>

04:00.002 --> 04:01.722
<i>With one exception—me.</i>

04:10.138 --> 04:12.115
My name is Hazama Kuroo.

04:12.473 --> 04:14.599
The teachers have given up on me,

04:14.600 --> 04:16.977
and other students are scared of getting close to me.

04:17.895 --> 04:21.440
I heard it's because I skip worthless classes,

04:21.441 --> 04:24.818
or that I have cruel-looking eyes.

04:24.819 --> 04:26.778
It really doesn't bother me.

04:26.779 --> 04:28.739
Hazama-kun!

04:28.740 --> 04:30.907
But this guy does.

04:31.868 --> 04:33.160
Good morning, Hazama-kun.

04:36.456 --> 04:38.415
Hazama-kun, good morning.

04:38.791 --> 04:40.167
Don't talk to me.

04:40.293 --> 04:44.390
Oh, come on. I'm just saying good morning.

04:44.630 --> 04:47.049
And it's annoying me.

04:47.175 --> 04:49.668
You're no fun.

04:50.636 --> 04:55.264
Hey Hazama-kun, don't you get tired
of having that frowny face all day?

04:55.433 --> 04:59.238
And don't you get tired of laughing?

04:59.802 --> 05:01.021
I don't!

05:01.022 --> 05:03.148
Besides, laughing is good for you.

05:07.904 --> 05:09.386
Don't get involved with me.

05:09.864 --> 05:12.282
We live in two different worlds.

05:14.327 --> 05:15.535
You think so?

05:15.536 --> 05:17.245
I think we're in the same one.

05:19.624 --> 05:20.999
What the...

05:29.384 --> 05:30.759
<i>It couldn't be the same.</i>

05:30.760 --> 05:33.428
<i>He's just always laughing.</i>

05:33.429 --> 05:36.515
<i>Or is he hiding something?</i>

05:40.311 --> 05:43.605
<i>I'm sure he has moments where he won't laugh too.</i>

05:44.232 --> 05:47.109
<i>I'll find out his secret!</i>

05:54.701 --> 05:55.948
Is something the matter?

05:56.202 --> 05:57.661
Oh...

05:59.914 --> 06:03.709
Oh, you mean Ueto Sho-kun?

06:03.710 --> 06:05.627
He's an unfortunate kid.

06:07.004 --> 06:09.131
His parents were deep in debt,

06:09.132 --> 06:12.371
so they skipped town, leaving him behind.

06:12.593 --> 06:16.221
But he's still hanging in there.

06:16.222 --> 06:17.806
Such a good kid.

06:17.807 --> 06:22.822
He waits for his parents to return, never
knowing when they'll be back.

06:31.612 --> 06:34.781
Mr. Principal, a real pal!

06:35.742 --> 06:36.551
I need to talk to you.

06:37.738 --> 06:38.559
Come with me.

06:41.289 --> 06:43.711
What's so funny?

06:44.000 --> 06:46.418
Well, I wonder what.

06:46.638 --> 06:49.254
I heard your parents skipped town.

06:49.255 --> 06:51.738
That happened a long time ago.

06:53.051 --> 06:54.521
Then how can you be laughing?!

06:54.761 --> 06:56.155
Why won't you get mad?!

06:57.379 --> 06:58.882
Don't you hate your parents for doing that to you?!

06:59.278 --> 07:00.138
Why?

07:00.657 --> 07:02.003
Why...

07:02.602 --> 07:04.686
They abandoned you!

07:04.687 --> 07:06.688
Yeah, but still...

07:07.315 --> 07:10.126
Crying is useless.

07:10.485 --> 07:12.694
Getting angry only leaves you feeling tired.

07:13.102 --> 07:15.197
Are you serious about this?

07:15.298 --> 07:16.337
Yeah.

07:17.097 --> 07:18.784
Are you out of your mind?!

07:18.785 --> 07:24.416
Anyone in their right mind would
be in despair in that situation!

07:24.935 --> 07:27.334
But here you are, laughing every day...

07:27.335 --> 07:29.439
That can't possibly be right!

07:31.706 --> 07:33.632
What's wrong with you?!

07:45.978 --> 07:47.688
I can't...

07:48.981 --> 07:50.709
possibly do that.

07:54.278 --> 07:58.971
<i>At that moment, I thought about the accident
that my mother and I were in,</i>

07:59.409 --> 08:01.842
<i>and, before I realized it, I had told him everything.</i>

08:04.330 --> 08:05.747
Mom!

08:48.278 --> 08:50.292
Mom!

08:51.711 --> 08:54.785
<i>About my mother, who protected
me from that undetonated bomb;</i>

08:56.424 --> 08:59.092
<i>about myself, who recovered from the near-fatal injury;</i>

09:00.505 --> 09:04.816
<i>about my father, who abandoned my mother
and left the country with another woman;</i>

09:05.475 --> 09:09.269
<i>and how ever since then, I was unable to laugh or smile.</i>

09:09.589 --> 09:13.461
<i>But he saved me from that.</i>

09:14.484 --> 09:15.613
Stand up.

09:18.654 --> 09:21.480
It's not good to be depressed.

09:23.993 --> 09:24.743
Shut up!

09:24.786 --> 09:25.827
I'm...

09:27.121 --> 09:28.217
I'm different than you.

09:28.873 --> 09:31.708
I don't laugh and just let everything go.

09:32.502 --> 09:35.017
And I've lived ever since that day to get revenge.

09:35.630 --> 09:39.838
I'll make the people who made me go through this pay.

09:41.386 --> 09:43.136
What a waste.

09:43.971 --> 09:44.860
What do you mean?

09:45.181 --> 09:50.102
A really good surgeon saved your life.

09:50.895 --> 09:54.398
Your life was ruined too!

09:55.441 --> 09:58.402
But do you know about family suicides?

09:58.403 --> 10:03.865
Compared to that, I'm really grateful
that they kept me alive.

10:04.516 --> 10:06.079
Y-You...

10:06.676 --> 10:07.470
Why...

10:07.954 --> 10:09.746
More importantly...

10:11.457 --> 10:14.680
Why won't you laugh?

10:17.046 --> 10:19.381
<i>He's really...</i>

10:24.137 --> 10:26.722
Hazama-kun, you have a funny face!

10:31.019 --> 10:37.182
<i>And since that day, two people with opposite
personalities and lifestyles started feeling closer,</i>

10:37.442 --> 10:39.276
<i>and started spending time together.</i>

10:46.533 --> 10:47.282
Sorry!

10:50.496 --> 10:53.123
Aim a little higher than where you feel it should be.

10:53.124 --> 10:53.707
There!

11:33.247 --> 11:34.998
Gera, you there?

11:36.626 --> 11:37.709
Hey!

11:38.294 --> 11:39.169
Here.

11:40.117 --> 11:42.464
I brought you a dart set.

11:43.093 --> 11:46.381
You said the other day that you wanted to get better.

11:46.803 --> 11:48.105
Thanks.

11:48.554 --> 11:52.350
Practice with that, so I won't have to hold back.

11:53.351 --> 11:54.434
This is great!

11:54.769 --> 12:00.146
But the debt collectors might take a nice set like this away.

12:01.275 --> 12:03.068
They're that cruel?

12:03.069 --> 12:04.569
They can't help it.

12:04.570 --> 12:06.071
They're only doing their job.

12:11.202 --> 12:12.391
Is that manga?

12:12.787 --> 12:13.936
Did you draw this?

12:14.146 --> 12:16.124
Mr. Principal: A Real Pal

12:18.084 --> 12:19.584
Not bad at all.

12:20.211 --> 12:23.459
I want to be a manga artist,

12:23.840 --> 12:28.593
and write manga that will make everyone laugh.

12:29.554 --> 12:31.251
You? A manga artist?

12:31.745 --> 12:35.434
You see, I can draw as long as I have paper and a pen.

12:42.984 --> 12:44.154
Is it weird?

12:44.658 --> 12:45.963
Not at all.

12:46.154 --> 12:48.321
Actually, might be a big hit.

12:48.948 --> 12:50.198
You think so?

12:50.199 --> 12:52.111
Yeah, a hit for sure!

12:55.663 --> 12:56.962
You finally smiled.

12:58.332 --> 13:02.004
I heard that only humans are capable
of smiling and laughing.

13:02.545 --> 13:05.797
The ability to laugh is a sign of intelligence.

13:06.799 --> 13:08.258
I see...

13:10.428 --> 13:13.221
Hey, is that manga funny?

13:13.931 --> 13:14.582
Yeah.

13:14.891 --> 13:15.833
It's the best.

13:16.100 --> 13:18.077
Then why won't you laugh?

13:20.034 --> 13:21.234
Come on, laugh!

13:28.780 --> 13:30.585
Is it really that funny?

13:30.782 --> 13:32.304
No, no!

13:34.077 --> 13:36.912
Well, it is funny, but it's more that I'm just happy!

13:37.747 --> 13:39.681
Excuse us.

13:53.554 --> 13:55.514
Who are you?

13:55.760 --> 13:57.307
And who are you?

13:57.308 --> 13:58.892
His friend?

13:59.477 --> 14:01.895
These people are the debt collectors.

14:02.021 --> 14:02.831
These people are...

14:03.161 --> 14:04.940
We are.

14:04.941 --> 14:06.817
So stay clear if you don't wanna get hurt.

14:08.611 --> 14:13.323
Hey man, have you heard from mommy or daddy?

14:13.324 --> 14:14.533
Not at all!

14:14.534 --> 14:16.743
I'd be happier if I had.

14:16.744 --> 14:20.622
Huh? But we heard laughter.

14:20.623 --> 14:22.874
You really did hear from them, didn't you?

14:22.875 --> 14:25.669
I'm not lying!

14:25.670 --> 14:28.839
You're always laughing.

14:28.840 --> 14:30.424
That pisses me off!

14:30.425 --> 14:31.633
Why...

14:31.634 --> 14:34.219
Hey, play with him a little.

14:34.220 --> 14:35.470
Hear that?

14:35.471 --> 14:37.681
So tell us, where's your dad?

14:37.682 --> 14:38.974
Spit it out!

14:38.975 --> 14:42.352
We're losing a ton of money because of him!

14:47.316 --> 14:48.191
Stop it!

14:48.192 --> 14:49.026
Get off!

14:49.068 --> 14:49.985
Stay off!

14:50.611 --> 14:52.195
Tell us now.

14:52.196 --> 14:55.279
Or else we'll break a few of your fingers.

14:55.550 --> 14:56.093
Stop it!

14:56.117 --> 14:58.035
If you do...

15:04.500 --> 15:07.627
Damn, you brat!

15:07.628 --> 15:08.837
Die!

15:08.838 --> 15:10.881
Stop it!

15:14.840 --> 15:15.628
Gera!

15:16.674 --> 15:17.531
Idiot!

15:17.555 --> 15:18.846
Look what you did!

15:18.973 --> 15:19.931
We're outta here!

15:26.040 --> 15:26.607
Gera!

15:26.981 --> 15:28.106
Gera!

15:34.739 --> 15:35.597
Slowly!

15:35.782 --> 15:36.698
Don't move him.

15:36.699 --> 15:37.881
He has cyanosis.

15:38.242 --> 15:40.285
It shouldn’t be fatal, but...

15:40.286 --> 15:41.620
Stabbed by a dart?

15:41.621 --> 15:42.659
How?!

15:49.504 --> 15:50.940
<i>It's all my fault.</i>

15:51.381 --> 15:53.977
<i>If I hadn't brought that dart set...</i>

15:56.094 --> 15:59.343
<i>Ever since then, his laughter was no longer heard,</i>

15:59.681 --> 16:03.767
<i>and the school felt cold and empty, as if it lost its flame.</i>

16:05.478 --> 16:09.022
<i>Gera's recovery from the hole in
his mediastinum did not go well,</i>

16:09.023 --> 16:11.850
<i>so the emergency medical center
transferred him to a hospital in the suburbs.</i>

16:12.568 --> 16:17.698
<i>Then I heard that he was transferred again—this
time to a remote place far away.</i>

16:20.493 --> 16:24.162
<i>News on Gera's condition stopped coming in after that.</i>

16:25.459 --> 16:29.126
<i>I went to a remote university to study medicine,</i>

16:29.127 --> 16:30.711
<i>and a few years had passed.</i>

16:33.631 --> 16:36.372
<i>Gera, I've studied medicine.</i>

16:36.759 --> 16:37.960
<i>Now, I can...</i>

16:38.469 --> 16:39.678
<i>I can...</i>

16:51.816 --> 16:53.224
<i>And finally...</i>

16:56.237 --> 16:57.779
I found you, Gera.

17:00.950 --> 17:02.805
Hey you.

17:03.453 --> 17:05.267
Long time no see.

17:06.100 --> 17:07.466
<i>Look at how bad he looks.</i>

17:07.915 --> 17:09.641
<i>Is this really him?</i>

17:11.002 --> 17:14.629
Gera, I've been eager for this day to come.

17:15.091 --> 17:18.791
I've studied medicine, so I could treat you myself.

17:19.218 --> 17:21.761
I'm finally good enough to do that.

17:28.811 --> 17:31.593
He cannot speak much,

17:31.814 --> 17:34.465
since it makes it difficult for him to breathe.

17:34.734 --> 17:39.613
And because of an old injury, he
now has mediastinal emphysema.

17:40.024 --> 17:44.316
When that happens, the patient goes into cyanosis
and goes through a great deal of pain.

17:44.494 --> 17:48.855
He's been in this condition for years now.

17:49.123 --> 17:50.567
It must have been tough for him.

17:52.543 --> 17:56.219
That patient once had chronic laughter.

17:57.632 --> 17:59.341
Chronic laughter?!

17:59.342 --> 18:00.634
Far from it!

18:00.635 --> 18:03.895
He's not laughed even once.

18:04.299 --> 18:06.908
If he does, he'll fall into cyanosis immediately.

18:08.378 --> 18:09.378
I see.

18:12.063 --> 18:13.480
Hang in there, Gera.

18:13.481 --> 18:15.927
I'll make it so you can laugh like you used to.

18:17.276 --> 18:18.792
Y-Yeah...

18:20.738 --> 18:22.259
The object of this operation is a scar.

18:22.532 --> 18:26.868
It is a chronically torn area from an injury
he sustained several years ago.

18:27.048 --> 18:28.787
All stitching in the past was ineffective,

18:28.788 --> 18:30.589
so we will use an artificial bronchus.

18:32.065 --> 18:32.719
Scalpel.

18:35.211 --> 18:37.671
Removing the fifth and sixth ribs and the sternum.

18:54.856 --> 18:56.314
Switch to the artificial heart-lung.

18:56.315 --> 18:57.941
I will complete the removal in five minutes.

18:58.317 --> 18:59.609
Artificial bronchus.

19:11.080 --> 19:12.453
Are you awake?

19:16.795 --> 19:18.434
The operation was successful.

19:18.713 --> 19:20.074
You'll be fine now.

19:20.677 --> 19:23.675
Gera, be a manga artist when you get well.

19:23.951 --> 19:28.096
Spread true laughter to people all around
Japan and all around the world!

19:28.514 --> 19:29.765
Yeah.

19:30.266 --> 19:34.414
You once said that only intelligent animals can laugh.

19:38.041 --> 19:42.311
I've finally started to become one
of those intelligent beings.

19:45.656 --> 19:48.210
Thank you.

19:51.564 --> 19:52.151
Take care.

20:05.349 --> 20:05.742
Hello.

20:07.011 --> 20:08.679
One moment please.

20:12.975 --> 20:14.822
What?! Gera did?!

20:17.772 --> 20:18.855
Yes.

20:19.148 --> 20:22.651
The patient passed away just moments ago.

20:25.279 --> 20:26.306
It was unfortunate.

20:26.656 --> 20:29.574
He was suffering from a severe
fever induced by pneumonia.

20:29.956 --> 20:32.410
He then died from septic shock.

20:32.620 --> 20:33.634
Death from shock...

20:37.709 --> 20:40.210
Perhaps he could sense his death approaching.

20:40.211 --> 20:43.772
He started laughing abruptly, despite the severe fever.

20:50.722 --> 20:55.598
His laughter was very bright and it echoed very far.

20:56.060 --> 20:58.167
It was even audible outside of the building,

20:58.396 --> 21:01.319
and even stopped the birds' chirping for a moment.

21:02.525 --> 21:05.548
I've never heard such great, honest laughter before.

21:10.908 --> 21:14.872
And after he stopped laughing, he
stopped breathing within seconds.

21:15.841 --> 21:18.252
He could laugh because of you.

22:10.544 --> 22:17.550
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.544 --> 22:17.550
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.551 --> 22:24.723
Only look straight at me.

22:17.551 --> 22:24.723
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.768 --> 22:32.025
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.768 --> 22:32.025
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:32.026 --> 22:42.535
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:32.026 --> 22:42.535
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.536 --> 22:47.916
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.536 --> 22:47.916
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.917 --> 22:57.300
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.917 --> 22:53.122
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.577 --> 22:57.301
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.301 --> 23:08.061
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.301 --> 23:08.061
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.062 --> 23:13.149
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.062 --> 23:13.149
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.150 --> 23:26.120
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.150 --> 23:26.120
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.121 --> 23:33.044
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.121 --> 23:33.044
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:33.045 --> 23:43.930
just as it was lead by the light.

23:33.045 --> 23:36.978
sora no hate tooku

23:37.071 --> 23:43.871
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.124 --> 24:15.126
Bouncer at the Culture Festival

23:45.277 --> 23:46.110
Thank you!

23:47.104 --> 23:47.815
Jaws?

23:47.870 --> 23:48.657
Come on.

23:54.277 --> 23:56.226
I want to live a cool life.

23:56.697 --> 24:01.129
If you get hot-blooded and pick a fight again,
your heart will almost certainly stop.

24:01.242 --> 24:04.688
Jaws is well-known for causing trouble at
culture festivals in this area.

24:05.355 --> 24:06.015
No way...

24:06.147 --> 24:07.600
Hurry up and save my son!

24:07.754 --> 24:10.894
What's so fun about bullying the weak?

24:11.614 --> 24:14.281
